TEXT 0 -352 Left 2 ;Problem 4.1 - bass-reflex box (lecture-3 box: vent 12 cm long, 10 cm diameter, 23 L) driven by a massless baffled piston of the vent's size
TEXT 0 -320 Left 2 ;mechanical MOBILITY (V_u = velocity u = 1 m/s), acoustic IMPEDANCE.  G1 pushes U = S*u from the back node pb into the front node pf
TEXT 0 -272 Left 2 !.param rho=1.18 c=344 a=0.05 l=0.12 V=0.023 S={pi*a**2}
TEXT 0 -240 Left 2 !.param Ma={rho*l/S} Ca={V/(rho*c**2)} Ma1={8*rho/(3*pi**2*a)} Ra1={0.441*rho*c/S} Ra2={rho*c/S} Ca1={5.94*a**3/(rho*c**2)}
TEXT 256 208 Left 2 ;G2: f = S*p (reaction force;
TEXT 256 240 Left 2 ;no effect, u is imposed)
TEXT 0 640 Left 2 !.ac dec 2000 10 20k
TEXT 0 688 Left 2 ;c) Z_A = p/U seen by the piston: plot (V(pf)-V(pb))/I(G1).  Peak (box-vent anti-resonance) near 79 Hz, not 92 Hz: the vent's outer radiation mass adds to M_A
TEXT 0 720 Left 2 ;front pressure V(pf), box pressure V(pb), vent mouth V(pv).  Vent volume velocity = V(pv) through the outer Z_ar;  official: Z_A,max = 995e3 Pa s/m^3
